<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN BELGOLAISE GETS NEW CHAIRMAN, MD.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN BELGOLAISE GETS NEW CHAIRMAN, MD.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Belgolaise, the African banking arm of Generale Bank , said on Thursday Managing Director Marc-Yves Blanpain would replace Michel Isralson as Chairman of the board of directors from this year's annual shareholders meeting.</p>
<p>Filip Dierckx, who has been with Generale Bank since 1983, would replace Blanpain as Managing Director.</p>
<p>Belgolaise, which is 55 percent owned by Generale Bank, has banking interests in 17 sub-Saharan African countries.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
